    description: "F74.A1 (blind severity 3/Moderate; primarily a positive global-bounding measurement; F74.A2 src/dst placeholder-asymmetry EXTENSION folded here). A substrate-wide partition of all 110533 edges by endpoint resolution: 72.75% (80416) close to two real non-placeholder nodes; 27.23% (30094) have a dst that resolves only to an external_symbol placeholder (src real); exactly 0.02% (23) truly dangling — ALL on the src side; 0% truly-dangling dst. Mechanism behind the asymmetry: boundary-synthesis materializes every unresolved DST as a placeholder node (dst side fully closed by construction) but there is NO symmetric SRC-side synthesis, so the 23 tier-4-filtered source ids have no placeholder fallback and remain literally absent. Placeholders cushion dst but serve as src in 0 edges. The spec_validator reports zero violations and has no dangling-endpoint check, so the 23 pass clean. This SUBSUMES (but is distinct-fix from) the 23-edge tier-4 src-drop (INV-jukok) and the validator-all-zero (WI-moriz). Fix: validator gains a dangling-endpoint check so the 23 src-dangling edges surface; src side handled symmetrically with dst (placeholder synthesis or edge suppression). filed via tranch 04 (methodology-comparability run, reused tranch-03 substrate sha a32c4a31)."  # 4988
